  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan Ecumenical Forum 2010</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sudan Ecumenical Forum (SEF) have a 3-year strategic plan, addressing the following key advocacy issues: 1) Promotion of the letter and spirit of the CPA; 2) Ensure that  the CPA is not overshadowed by Darfur and to ensure a balanced &#x201c;whole country&#x201d; approach; 3) Address the Darfur conflict in the context of the whole country and the region, and apply lessons learned from dealing with the war in south; 4) Draw attention to other potential conflict flashpoints; 5) Provision of adequate response to the needs of the people; 6) Promote and encourage reconciliation and healing on different levels. The total project budget covers the Sudan Focal Point (SFP) Europe and the SFP Africa (to be recruited); SEF Core Group (3 per year) and General Assemblies (every 18 months); SEF operational costs; and Administrative Agency costs.</narrative>
  </description>
